AWS Load Balancer Controller
===========================
Application EKS
      |
      ↓
AWS Load Balancer Controller
      |
      ↓
Application Frontend LB



Monitoring EKS
      |
      ↓
AWS Load Balancer Controller
      |
      +----> Grafana public LB
      |
      +----> Prometheus internal NLB
      |
      +----> Loki internal NLB
      |
      +----> Tempo internal NLB

so we have to install load balancer controller on both the clusters.
application-eks
       |
       └── AWS Load Balancer Controller

monitoring-eks
       |
       └── AWS Load Balancer Controller


First verify AWS CLI identity

aws sts get-caller-identity

Verify OIDC for Application EKS

aws eks describe-cluster \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --name application-eks \
  --query 'cluster.identity.oidc.issuer' \
  --output text

Expected:
https://oidc.eks.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/id/XXXXXXXX

aws eks describe-cluster \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --name monitoring-eks \
  --query 'cluster.identity.oidc.issuer' \
  --output text

Check whether the AWS Load Balancer Controller policy already exists
aws iam get-policy \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):policy/AWSLoadBalancerControllerIAMPolicy


Install Helm repository
helm repo add eks https://aws.github.io/eks-charts
helm repo update
helm search repo eks/aws-load-balancer-controller

Create the IAM policy if its not exit

Download the current AWS policy:
curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes-sigs/aws-load-balancer-controller/main/docs/install/iam_policy.json

Create policy:
aws iam create-policy \
  --policy-name AWSLoadBalancerControllerIAMPolicy \
  --policy-document file://iam_policy.json

Verify:
aws iam get-policy \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):policy/AWSLoadBalancerControllerIAMPolicy


Create Monitoring IAM service account for monitoring EKS

eksctl create iamserviceaccount \
  --cluster monitoring-eks \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --namespace kube-system \
  --name aws-load-balancer-controller \
  --role-name AmazonEKSLoadBalancerControllerRole-monitoring \
  --attach-policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):policy/AWSLoadBalancerControllerIAMPolicy \
  --approve

Install controller in Monitoring EKS

helm upgrade --install aws-load-balancer-controller \
  eks/aws-load-balancer-controller \
  -n kube-system \
  --set clusterName=monitoring-eks \
  --set serviceAccount.create=false \
  --set serviceAccount.name=aws-load-balancer-controller \
  --set region=ap-south-1 \
  --set vpcId="$MON_VPC_ID"

kubectl get pods \
  -n kube-system \
  -l app.kubernetes.io/name=aws-load-balancer-controller

kubectl get deployment \
  aws-load-balancer-controller \
  -n kube-system

Switch to Application EKS:

kubectl config use-context application-eks

Create IAM service account for Application EKS:
eksctl create iamserviceaccount \
  --cluster application-eks \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --namespace kube-system \
  --name aws-load-balancer-controller \
  --role-name AmazonEKSLoadBalancerControllerRole-application \
  --attach-policy-arn arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):policy/AWSLoadBalancerControllerIAMPolicy \
  --approve

AWS IAM
   |
   ↓
AmazonEKSLoadBalancerControllerRole-application
   |
   ↓
Kubernetes ServiceAccount
aws-load-balancer-controller
   |
   ↓
AWS Load Balancer Controller

kubectl get serviceaccount \
  aws-load-balancer-controller \
  -n kube-system

Install AWS Load Balancer Controller

helm upgrade --install aws-load-balancer-controller \
  eks/aws-load-balancer-controller \
  -n kube-system \
  --set clusterName=application-eks \
  --set serviceAccount.create=false \
  --set serviceAccount.name=aws-load-balancer-controller \
  --set region=ap-south-1 \
  --set vpcId="$APP_VPC_ID"

kubectl get pods \
  -n kube-system \
  -l app.kubernetes.io/name=aws-load-balancer-controller

